stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 720 Td 16 TL
(Aurora Brew 3000 - User Manual \(Part 3: Maintenance & Troubleshooting\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Daily cleaning) Tj T*
(- Empty the used coffee grounds and rinse the filter basket.) Tj T*
(- Wash the carafe and lid with warm soapy water after each use.) Tj T*
(- Wipe the warming plate with a damp cloth once the machine is cool.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Descaling) Tj T*
(Descale the machine every 60 brews or every 3 months, whichever comes first.) Tj T*
(1. Fill the reservoir with a mixture of one part white vinegar and two parts water.) Tj T*
(2. Place a carafe in position and run a full brew cycle without coffee.) Tj T*
(3. Discard the liquid and run two more cycles with clean water.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Water filter replacement) Tj T*
(Replace the built-in carbon filter every 90 days or every 100 brews.) Tj T*
(The filter indicator light on the control panel will flash when a replacement is due.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Troubleshooting) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Problem: Machine does not turn on.) Tj T*
(Cause: No power, or the power cord is not fully seated.) Tj T*
(Fix: Check the outlet and the cord connection. Reset the circuit breaker.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Problem: Coffee is too weak.) Tj T*
(Cause: Not enough coffee grounds, or the brew-strength selector is set to Mild.) Tj T*
(Fix: Increase the amount of coffee or select the Strong brew setting.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Problem: Brewing is slow.) Tj T*
(Cause: The machine needs descaling.) Tj T*
(Fix: Run the descaling procedure described above.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Problem: Coffee tastes bitter.) Tj T*
(Cause: The carafe was left on the warming plate for more than 2 hours.) Tj T*
(Fix: Use the pause-and-serve function and do not reheat coffee.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Technical support) Tj T*
(Contact Aurora customer care at support@aurorabrew.example or call +1-800-555-AURORA.) Tj T*
(Have your serial number ready. The serial number is located on the underside.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
